Fix Lua garbage collector use-after-free on scripting reset (CVE-2024-46981)

SCRIPT FLUSH (and the reset on FLUSHALL/DEBUG RELOAD paths) tears the Lua VM
down with lua_close(). Lua runs pending __gc finalizers during close while its
GC state still references objects that user scripts can have arranged to be
freed early, giving a use-after-free that an authenticated client can steer
into remote code execution. Running a full collection (LUA_GCCOLLECT) before
lua_close() resets the GC state so nothing reachable from destructor callbacks
is freed prematurely.

Tracker: CVE-2024-46981
Upstream patch: https://github.com/redis/redis/commit/ca0a9ab822dcd6d6ec6e2b6dd3a7d7b0dd8fc912
Adaptation: src/scripting.c renamed to src/scripting.cpp in KeyDB; the global
server struct is reached through g_pserver-> instead of server. in KeyDB, so
the inserted lua_gc() call uses g_pserver->lua. Fix logic unchanged.

diff --git a/src/scripting.cpp b/src/scripting.cpp
--- a/src/scripting.cpp
+++ b/src/scripting.cpp
@@ -1330,6 +1330,7 @@ void scriptingRelease(int async) {
     else
         dictRelease(g_pserver->lua_scripts);
     g_pserver->lua_scripts_mem = 0;
+    lua_gc(g_pserver->lua, LUA_GCCOLLECT, 0);
     lua_close(g_pserver->lua);
 }
 
